  "term": "alcohol use disorder",
  "definition": "Alcohol use disorder is a psychiatric disorder involving alcohol-related symptoms such as craving and problematic patterns of alcohol use. It is a major contributor to the global burden of mental illness and often occurs together with post-traumatic stress disorder.",
